From: Seth Morris <sethmorris.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:43:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Initialize preferred audio devices on construction

The default sink and source change signals may be emitted before
PreferredDevice is constructed. In that case, the preferred devices
remain unset until the defaults change again.

Initialize both devices in the constructor so the existing defaults
are available immediately.

BUG: 500828
BUG: 521973
FIXED-IN: 6.8.0
Origin: upstream, https://invent.kde.org/plasma/plasma-pa/-/commit/eaeaa6a9a2142b8eae067f3028a43bfaf38414f3
Forwarded: not-needed
Bug: https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=500828
---
 src/preferreddevice.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/src/preferreddevice.cpp
+++ b/src/preferreddevice.cpp
@@ -69,6 +69,9 @@ PreferredDevice::PreferredDevice(QObject *parent)
     });
     connect(PulseAudioQt::Context::instance(), &PulseAudioQt::Context::sourceRemoved, this, &PreferredDevice::updatePreferredSource);
     connect(PulseAudioQt::Context::instance()->server(), &PulseAudioQt::Server::defaultSourceChanged, this, &PreferredDevice::updatePreferredSource);
+
+    updatePreferredSink();
+    updatePreferredSource();
 }
 
 PulseAudioQt::Sink *PreferredDevice::sink() const
